# Read an already accepted real context. No credentials, jobs or ledger resets.
name: Accepted threat model remains distinct from optional repository index
size: 120x36
cwd: @TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/live_context_receipts.py @TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 accepted | accepted-map
expect: Map ✓
expect: repo index not built
expect: repo index:missing
expect: changing its title.
expect-not: context not built
ask: Does the accepted threat model show its full system description and distinct optional repository-index absence without prompting context regeneration?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | accepted-160x48
expect: SESSION COST
expect: No spend recorded
expect: session dollar cap unset
expect: report · prior usage
expect-not: $0.00 spent
expect-not: budget not enforced
ask: Does the fresh shell scope its session accounting and direct prior investigation usage to Report without implying zero lifetime spend or unenforced request limits?
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | accepted-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | accepted-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | accepted-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | accepted-40x12
expect: accepted
expect: This repository
expect-not: context not built
ask: At 40x12, does the accepted Map show actual system context with paging controls instead of spending its reading space on empty borders?
keys: PageUp
require-live-snap: 20 This repository | summary-start-boundary-40x12
keys: PageDown
require-live-snap: 20 private notes | summary-page-40x12
ask: Does one Page Down expose the next contiguous context rows while the composer, acceptance and Summary tab remain intact?
keys: PageUp
require-live-snap: 20 This repository | summary-return-40x12
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 app.py note functions | selected-component-40x12
ask: Can the operator select the next component at 40x12 and see its identity without changing the accepted context or starting work?
resize: 120x36
require-live-snap: 20 repo index not built | restored-wide-status
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 accepted | accepted-no-color
expect: repo index not built
expect: repo index:missing
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/live_context_receipts.py @TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain accepted context and honest index status with unchanged source, seven live requests and two protected Review requests?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
